From 03eba92b90ddc3f6051db29e9054e475c92ffa91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:00:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: copy into the limited range of the
 framebuffer's depth

dvbridge_gl_copy() put a picture into the limited range of an RGB signal with
the 10-bit range (64 to 940 of 1023) at every depth. In an 8-bit framebuffer
that made white 234 (940/1023 of 255, rounded) instead of 235: a picture
rebuilt as HDR10 in an 8-bit window with "Use limited colour range" on had its
top code one low. The range is now that of the target's depth, 16 to 235 times
2^(n - 8) of 2^n - 1. A 10-bit target and a floating-point one get exactly what
they got: the same expression is kept for them.

Measured on the software OpenGL ES (zink on lavapipe), a rebuilt profile 5
chart copied to 8- and 10-bit framebuffers, full and limited range: every value
at its nearest code; before, 1342085 values of the 8-bit limited copy were one
code off, and none of the others. The render test of the bridge on the FEL test
stream (both ways of native output, the picture for output as HDR10 and its
copies, and the mapping to a display) gives the same output, line for line, as
before.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c | 11 +++++++++--
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.h |  6 ++++--
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c
index c4d34a5..51b9e73 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c
@@ -187,7 +187,11 @@ static const char COPY_VERTEX[] =
  * is written 1/256 of a step above its value. A framebuffer that rounds what it is given makes
  * that level of it, and so does one that cuts it off, also the one that makes 10 bits by
  * dropping six of 16, whose steps are a little narrower (a software renderer does that: written
- * 1/64 of a step above their value, the levels from 1015 on came out one too high there). */
+ * 1/64 of a step above their value, the levels from 1015 on came out one too high there).
+ * Hades: the limited range is that of the target's depth: 16 to 235 times 2^(n - 8) of 2^n - 1
+ * (64 to 940 of 1023 at 10 bits, 16 to 235 of 255 at 8). The range of 10 bits was taken for all,
+ * which put the white of an 8-bit target at 234 and its black at 16, the white 1 code low. A
+ * 10-bit target, and a floating-point one, get what they always got. */
 static const char COPY_FRAGMENT[] =
     "#version 300 es\n"
     "precision highp float;\n"
@@ -202,7 +206,10 @@ static const char COPY_FRAGMENT[] =
     "    if (flip_height > 0)\n"
     "        p.y = flip_height - 1 - p.y;\n"
     "    vec3 c = clamp(texelFetch(picture, p, 0).rgb, 0.0, 1.0);\n"
-    "    if (limited != 0)\n"
+    "    float step8 = (levels + 1.0) / 256.0;\n"
+    "    if (limited != 0 && levels > 0.0 && levels != 1023.0)\n"
+    "        c = (c * (219.0 * step8) + 16.0 * step8) / levels;\n"
+    "    else if (limited != 0)\n"
     "        c = (c * 876.0 + 64.0) / 1023.0;\n"
     "    if (levels > 0.0)\n"
     "        c = (floor(c * levels + 0.5) + 0.00390625) / levels;\n"
diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.h b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.h
index 18a0971..0aca921 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.h
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.h
@@ -27,8 +27,10 @@ bool dvbridge_gl_pack(struct dvbridge_gl_packer *packer, unsigned pq_texture,
  * value off (a software renderer's copy of one framebuffer to another did). A floating-point one
  * gets the values as they are. Only the rectangle given (from the top left) is written.
  * flip_y: the first row of the framebuffer is the bottom one, as in a window. limited: the
- * values go into the limited range of an RGB signal (64 to 940 of 1023), as those of Kodi's
- * video do when its output is set to that. The GL state is put back. */
+ * values go into the limited range of an RGB signal of the framebuffer's depth (64 to 940 of 1023,
+ * 16 to 235 of 255), as those of Kodi's video do when its output is set to that. The GL state is
+ * put back. */
+#define DVBRIDGE_GL_COPY_LIMITED_AT_DEPTH 1
 struct dvbridge_gl_copier;
 struct dvbridge_gl_copier *dvbridge_gl_copier_create(void);
 void dvbridge_gl_copier_destroy(struct dvbridge_gl_copier *copier);
-- 
2.53.0

